@node Install
@chapter Install

@cindex Install

If manually installed@comma{} ensure that @code{burnish.el} is in your @code{load-path}.

Add the following to your Emacs initialization file.

@lisp
(require 'burnish) ; optional if autoloaded
(burnish-bind)
@end lisp

@code{burnish-bind} will do the following:

@itemize
@item
Add the command @code{burnish} to the hook variable @code{after-save-hook}.
@item
Bind the command @code{burnish} to the key set in the variable @code{burnish-export-key} (default @code{C-<f5>}).
@end itemize

@node Usage
@chapter Usage

For @strong{Burnish} to work@comma{} it requires that the local file variable @code{burnish-backend} be defined in the Org file. The value of this variable is set to a target Org backend. By default@comma{}  @code{burnish-backend} supports the following values:

@itemize
@item
html — export to HTML
@item
md — export to Markdown
@item
odt — export to Open Office Doc
@item
latex — export to @LaTeX{}
@item
texinfo — export to Texinfo
@end itemize

An example of defining @code{burnish-backend} in an Org file is shown below@comma{} where this text is appended at the end of the file. For more detail on file variables@comma{} see @ref{Specifying File Variables,,,emacs,}.

@example

