@node Commands
@section Commands

@vindex burnish
@deffn Command burnish
Run the function that exports and views the Org file.

This function is specified by two variables:

@itemize
@item
@code{burnish-export-functions} — map containing (backend@comma{} export function) pairs.

@item
@code{burnish-backend} — local file variable specifying with backend to use.
@end itemize
@end deffn

@vindex burnish-bind
@deffn Command burnish-bind
Turn on automatic export and viewing of an Org file.

For an Org file that has the local file variable @code{burnish-backend} specified@comma{}

Configure Emacs to run @code{burnish} whenever an Org file with @code{burnish-backend} defined is saved.

This command also binds @code{burnish} to the key sequence specified by @code{burnish-export-key}.
@end deffn

@vindex burnish-unbind
@deffn Command burnish-unbind
Turn off automatic export and viewing of an Org file.

This command undoes all configuration done by @code{burnish-bind}.
@end deffn

@vindex burnish-select-backend
@deffn Command burnish-select-backend CHOICE
Set local variable ‘burnish-backend’ to CHOICE in Org file.

This command modifies the Org file to set the local file variable @code{burnish-backend} within it.

See @ref{Specifying File Variables,,,emacs,} for more detail on local file variables.

When run interactively@comma{} @code{burnish-select-backend} prompts the user for a backend (CHOICE) to use when exporting and viewing an Org file. The prompt supports completion whose choices are the backend keys defined in the customizable variable @code{burnish-export-functions}.
@end deffn

@node Customization
@section Customization

@cindex Customization

@defvar burnish-backend
Local file variable that must be set in an Org file for the @code{burnish} command to run.
@end defvar

@defopt @code{burnish-export-functions}
Alist of export backends and their corresponding functions.

Each element is a cons cell (SYMBOL . FUNCTION) where SYMBOL is an export backend and FUNCTION is its corresponding export function.

This variable can be amended to support additional export backends provided that an export function for the new backend is defined.
@end defopt

@defopt burnish-export-key
String used to define the key sequence to bind the command @code{burnish}. Default value @kbd{C-<f5>}.
@end defopt

